{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "הירא", :translit "ha-yarei", :gloss "the one who fears"} {:he "הירא ורך הלבב", :translit "ha-yarei v'rech ha-levav", :gloss "the one who fears and faint of heart"} {:he "הירא את דבר ה'", :translit "ha-yarei et dvar Hashem", :gloss "the one who feared the word of the LORD"} {:he "וירד עליהם הברד ומתו", :translit "va-yared aleihem ha-barad va-yamtu", :gloss "and the hail came down on them and they died"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["הירא" "הירא ורך הלבב"]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezera shava between two occurrences of הירא"}], :frame {:text "A gezera shava links two cases of הירא. In Deuteronomy 20:8, הירא ורך הלבב describes one who fears because of a transgression in his hand — he is sent home lest his fear demoralize others (Mishnah Sotah 8:5). The same logic applies here: in Exodus 9:20, הירא את דבר ה' is immediately followed by וירד עליהם הברד ומתו (Exodus 9:25), so these God-fearers too died in the plague, indicating that even the best of Egypt perished.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 20:8" "Exodus 9:20" "Exodus 9:25" "Mishnah Sotah 8:5"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["הירא" "הירא ורך הלבב"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "הירא", :refs ["Exodus 9:20" "Deuteronomy 20:8"], :n 2, :lens :exact} {:phrase "הירא ורך הלבב", :refs ["Deuteronomy 20:8"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezera shava between two occurrences of הירא", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:14:33.759965067Z", :model "glm-5.2"}